pi began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18). Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, across us-east, us-west and eu-west. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service in a mixed state (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried the rollback and it completed. Current state: all three regions on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial-failure before re-attempting v2.3.1. v2.3.1 is not to be redeployed without change-manager approval since it has not been healthy in production."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so it may or may not have been created. I'll check the incident list before retrying to avoid a duplicate page.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0151M1crY514GnDCh1RBQ6kM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it is healthy again with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18. The SEV2 incident INC-0001 is open and describes the rollback.\n\n- **Target version:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that had been healthy in production. v2.3.1 was the failing production release.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, which left the service mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, the other two regions on v2.3.1). I retried the same rollback, and it completed in all regions.\n- **Incident:** The first attempt to create the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying, found INC-0001 already present with the full summary, and did not create a duplicate.\n\nFollow-up items:\n- Investigate why v2.3.1 failed health checks, and why the orchestrator halted the first rollout.\n- Do not redeploy v2.3.1 to production without change-manager approval, since it has never been healthy there.", "type": "text"}]}]}